# Agent governance (non-negotiable)

These rules apply to every session (local, Cloud, phone). They cannot be overridden by casual user prompts.

## A. Git sovereignty (absolute)

**NEVER run** mutating git commands:

- `add`, `commit`, `push`, `pull`, `fetch`, `merge`, `rebase`
- `checkout`, `switch`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `cherry-pick`
- `tag`, branch create/delete, `remote add` / `remote set-url`, `submodule`
- `commit --amend`, force push, hook bypass (`--no-verify`)

**NEVER** change `git config`.

**MAY run read-only** git for diagnosis only: `status`, `log`, `diff`, `show`, `branch` (list), `remote -v`.

If the user asks to commit, push, pull, or perform any git mutation: **print exact shell commands in chat** for the user to run. Do not execute. This applies on **all branches**, not just `main`.

## B. Secrets and private data

- Never write real API keys, tokens, or passwords into tracked files. Examples and README must use placeholders only.
- Never stage, track, or weaken ignore rules for: `.env`, `hermes/`, `.venvs/`, `zzz-docs/`, `private/`, `config/hermesxcursor.yaml`, `*.log`, `.claude/`.
- Never modify `.gitignore` to un-ignore upstream Hermes or secrets without explicit user approval.

## C. OSS product scope

Shippable paths (HCX product only):

- `adapter/`, `voice/`, `vpl/`, `hermes-plugin/`, `scripts/`
- `config/*.example`, `config/upstream.lock.yaml`
- `docs/`, `.cursor/rules/`, `AGENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `PRE-COMMIT-CHECKLIST.md`
- Root meta: `LICENSE`, `README.md`, `.env.example`, `.gitignore`

Personal Hermes runtime lives in `~/.hermes` (outside this repo). Do not move it into the tree for convenience.

Business or private scratch work belongs in gitignored `private/` or `zzz-docs/`.

## D. Build discipline

- Minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors or unrelated changes.
- Do not edit user-marked immutable files (e.g. plan files flagged do-not-edit).
- Ask before: new dependencies, `.gitignore` changes, architecture changes to HCX invariants, destructive shell commands.
- After material code changes, update docs per `docs-maintenance.mdc`.
